Phase 6.6 — Alerts & Thresholds:-
===============================

Now we'll add a few useful alerts, without creating too many rules or putting unnecessary load on your small cluster.

We'll start with the most important one: node CPU > 80%.

In Grafana:

Alerting → Alert rules → New alert rule

Set the query:

"""
100 - (
  avg by (instance) (
    rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode="idle"}[5m])
  ) * 100
)
"""

Set the condition:

WHEN query A
IS ABOVE
80

Configure:

Evaluate every: 1m
For: 5m
Alert name: K3s Node CPU High

This means the alert fires only if a node stays above 80% CPU for 5 continuous minutes, avoiding noisy alerts from short spikes.

Add a second alert — Memory

Query:

100 * (
  1 -
  (
    node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes
    /
    node_memory_MemTotal_bytes
  )
)

Condition:

IS ABOVE 85

Name:

K3s Node Memory High

Use the same:

Evaluate every: 1m
For: 5m
Third alert — PostgreSQL Down

Query:

pg_up{job="postgres"}

Condition:

IS BELOW 1

Name:

PostgreSQL Down

For:

2m


